{"kind":"request","text":"Set E's three public contracts before surface edits. This is source-only preparation under d5fa31c9; B has not landed, so E implementation has not begun. C is on main. I read the parent and both amendments; latest176190 permits E source after B and C land while D finishes.\n\nProposed decisions:\n1. Add handle.intents.\u003ckind\u003e(signer, asked, signing?) for non-genesis declared acts. Each method reads a fresh summary, checks the declared/published digest, derives expected with A's expectedOf/viaLeft and bounded final-item reads, then uses the existing shape/sign path. Return the signed packet plus the derivation head, or the preserved read/definition/incomplete failure before calling the signer. Preserve explicit asked.expected as the caller's captured map; never refresh it silently. Keep generic intent and explicit submit unchanged. Names live under intents, so declared act names cannot replace handle members. No grant/state/guard availability claim; retry a kept packet through submit.\n2. formFor delegates wording and schema to B's description binding and retains typed declaration fields. Its caller supplies catalogue, pinned setting and standing context. slotsFor returns typed parties/values/refs declarations, without labels/live values/new nullability policy. actsOn returns sorted state candidates for existing items: transitions and item-bound comments, filtered only by unconditional primary-subject state guards. Opens/no-item comments stay out; other guards leave a candidate unknown. It hides neither methods nor MCP tools and establishes no authority. MCP identity/listing/output stays unchanged.\n3. expression(ctx) supplies a tag and typed .field(name)/.slot(subject,name) tokens, emitting existing fields and subjects.\u003calias\u003e.\u003cslot-group\u003e profile paths with proper quoting. Interpolation holes accept only those reference tokens, rather than the broad Operand union. Existing rule(name,string), hoisting, compile findings and restricted@1 admission remain. TypeScript checks token names; it does not check arbitrary raw template fragments. No operator/tree builder, evaluator, exposed program AST or new profile.\n\nConfirm or amend these contracts, especially sign-versus-submit, explicit expected/read-failure semantics, the actsOn kind/state policy, and the typed-template guarantee. The full read-only proposal with unrun examples is /private/tmp/artroom-r3b-evidence-dxt2-e-public-api-proposal-20261110.md, SHA96168b1fb43239d72859bc0954b54fa2ced87cbacd8c8886248ed36bc80f9f0c. No E promise, source change, new case, parser/compiler/test/capture/CI body or pin change has occurred.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the three proposed E public contracts before E surface edits. Preserve existing generic client, plain-data downstream boundary, unchanged profile/pins/catalogue and the accepted B+C source-start order.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}